description:
Battles for Quebec is Clash of Arms' tenth installment of the award-winning "Battles in the Age of Reason" (BAR) series. It includes three battles and seven scenarios.

The Plains of Abraham(13 september 1759). This includes the famous morning clash on the heights: Montcalm vs. Wolfe. It also includes a scenario that starts with the first British landing, in which gamers play out the entire day's battle and see what could have happened.

Sainte Foy (29 April 1760). Three scenarios represent this largely forgotten battle in which the French had one last chance to defeat the British and possibly retake Quebec. This is a classic BAR battle on the frozen plains outside Quebec.

Assault on Quebec (31 December 1775). In a very different battle for the series, American forces are trying to assault Quebec at night in a blizzard. The fate of the fourteenth colony is at stake. This close battle will challenge the most experienced BAR gamers, and includes a scenario with hiden forces for a complete fog of war experience.

Meticulously researched, including the use of primary sources to determine the delicatedeatils of the battles, Battles for Quebec is a thorough treatment of these battles, represented at a depth that has never been seen before in wargaming.

Components:

        BAR Standard Series Rules booklet (v3.4);
        Battles for Quebec game-specific rules booklet;
        Battles for Quebec game-specific charts and tables;
        One 22" x 34" full color, period-style map;
        420 1/2" Counters, both full color and black & white;
        Cardstock diagrams and displays;
        Two ten-sided dice.


&mdash;description from Clash of Arms website

In The Cozy Hut, you build a secluded hut deep in the forest and spend several months there, leaving behind the troubles and burdens of modern life. Long ago, the writer and philosopher Henry David Thoreau did the same: he lived alone in the woods by a pond called Walden for two years, two months, and two days. With his own hands, he built a small hut, planted garden beds, made a stove, and sealed the cracks with moss and clay. He brought from town only nails, lamp oil, and books. The world of nature and solitude gave Thoreau many wonderful discoveries &mdash; and the manuscript of what would become his masterpiece, &ldquo;Walden, or Life in the Woods.&rdquo;

Inspired by this beautiful book, this game invites you to capture the spirit of philosophical tranquility. Following in Thoreau&rsquo;s footsteps, you will build a small forest hut in search of warmth and inner peace. Perfection and comfort are not the goal here &mdash; something will always be missing. Your aim is a cozy hut: a place with a minimum for the body and a maximum for the soul.

&mdash;description from the designer

Background. Starting in the mid-1950s, Italy went through an unprecedented industrial and economic growth that lasted well into the mid-1960s. This period in Italian history is referred to as "Miracolo Economico Italiano" (Italian Economic Miracle) or "Boom Economico Italiano" (Italian Economic Boom).
&nbsp;
The economy runs at full speed, national income grows and people are employment rates reach new records. The reasons for this growth were the favorable international economic situation and the abundance of labor supply. Exports were also a major stimulus for the development of the country's industrial fabric.
&nbsp;
These years brought extraordinary transformations that affected the lifestyle and customs of Italians, accompanied by a marked increase in living standards. Numerous consumer goods, such as the first washing machines, the first refrigerators and the first television sets, began to enter the homes of Italian families, forever changing the lives of Italians.
&nbsp;
In Dolcissima Vita 2-4 players are entrerpreneurs who produce televisions, washing machines and refrigerators and sell them in Italy.
Most actions in the game are carried out by a very clever dice selection system. The sum of dice pips allows players to conduct basic and advanced actions, while dice colors let players advance on four different tracks (Workers, Scientific Research, Maintenance and Solidarity), which have various effects on the course of the game.
&nbsp;
Dolcissima Vita features 35 colorful Event Cards of Italian history from 1955 to 1968. These cards change the conditions of the game, either permanently or temporarily.
&nbsp;
Dolcissima Vita is the first volume in Spielworxx&acute; 'Italian Trilogy', dedicated to Italian history after World War II.

The alien invasion has begun, and humans are in a rush to escape Earth before it&rsquo;s too late! The only problem is that aliens are disguised as humans! Our only hope is to weed out the aliens via the power of &hellip; multiple choice questions!

While the aliens know how to blend in and look like us, they don&rsquo;t quite understand human culture. These questions are carefully crafted to help expose the space invaders. All you have to do is answer like any normal human would. It&rsquo;s that easy! It&rsquo;s only the fate of humanity at stake &hellip; Don&rsquo;t sweat it!

In Totally Human, players are given hidden identities (human or alien) and must answer three multiple-choice questions as "human-like" as possible, but aliens don't understand human culture completely and face restrictions on how they can respond.&nbsp;

The humans&rsquo; goal is to escape on the biggest alien-free rocket to form a new colony out in the stars.&nbsp;

The aliens&rsquo; goal is to blend in and sneak onto any rocket with humans for a tasty, post-invasion snack.&nbsp;

Both aliens and humans can achieve their goals on different rockets, but it's also possible that nobody wins. Be careful who you trust!

&mdash;description from the publisher

It&rsquo;s time to roll the dice! Friends of the card game Gigi Gacker will flock to the dice-pecker-worm buffet&thinsp;&hellip; and all young hens who love wormy appetisers.

Just 3 dice per player are enough to create a big cackle on the chicken menu board. At the start of each game round, a worm snack is laid out on the buffet for each player&thinsp;&ndash;&thinsp;in different sizes and flavours. According to the familiar Gigi Gacker game principle, the biggest&thinsp;&ndash;&thinsp;and now &lsquo;strongest&rsquo;&thinsp;&ndash;&thinsp;chicken always grabs the first morsel on the buffet&thinsp;&ndash;&thinsp;even if it is not the tastiest. In the dice rounds, all the &lsquo;tactical&nbsp;tricks&rsquo; are used to fight for the biggest morsels. Less tasty worms themselves can be used as &lsquo;dice substitutes&rsquo; or simply &lsquo;added&rsquo; to the neighbouring plates. It is also very popular to reverse the order of the courses on the buffet until the competition is at the very back. Apart from that, some starters are extremely inedible and carry minus points&thinsp;&hellip;

&mdash;description from the publisher

Patrol the streets, alleys and markets of Traitor&rsquo;s Toll. Chase down and arrest the rogues, cheats and cutthroats that prey on the unwary, ensure the citizens don&rsquo;t get too rebellious and uncover deeper plots that threaten the city&hellip;

The bustling city of Traitor&rsquo;s Toll is home to a multitude of merchants and travellers, buskers and charlatans, sorcerers and scholars, not to mention &ndash; hidden among them &ndash; pickpockets, thieves, smugglers and worse! The task of keeping the citizens safe, catching wrongdoers and dealing out justice falls to the city guard.

Gameplay is semi-cooperative. Both players control a Guard Captain and patrol of 5 guardsmen, who must deal with the many challenges hidden among the crowds. Such tasks might be capturing an escaped prisoner, battling a crazed wizard, locating a lost child, taking down a smuggling gang or investigating a mystery. While they have the same goals, each side is trying to make the most arrests, grab the glory and win recognition (and reward) from their superiors. Gain experience, recruit allies and locate useful items &ndash; the odd bribe will be useful too. A degree of violence will be necessary but killing suspects will upset the populace. If there is too much discontent, the people riot and rebel &ndash; the city lords will be furious (and both players lose)! The game has a strong narrative, legacy element as your guards develop new skills and learn secrets that impact subsequent tasks as well as later games.

&ldquo;Explore the ruined Imperial City of Metbetoch in search of lost secrets, powerful spells, and artifacts before your opponents can beat you to it!&rdquo;

Thematic scenario-based hexploration and area control game with quests and combat, where each player manages their party of adventurers improving skills, getting gear, and discovering secrets while fighting some of the most dangerous denizens that have infested the city's ruins and catacombs.

&mdash;description from the publisher

Greetings, Townsfolk! Your cosy hamlet recently welcomed three new dragon hatchlings, but there&rsquo;s not enough room for them in the watchtower where mother dragon has chosen to roost. Work together to manipulate the watchtower, to create safe spaces for the baby dragons and to settle the hatchlings in before mother dragon returns&hellip;

Working together, use tools to manipulate a tower of wooden pieces. Create enough space to safely balance 3 baby dragon miniatures before running out of tool actions. Finally, place the mother dragon on top of your tower to win. If any baby dragons fall, you lose (but don&rsquo;t worry; we put up a net to catch them!). Test your skills over dozens of levels with new tower structures and challenge tokens.

&mdash;description from the publisher

&ldquo;You will be haunted,&rdquo; said the Ghost of Jacob Marley, &ldquo;by Three Spirits.&rdquo;

&ldquo;I&mdash;I think I&rsquo;d rather not,&rdquo; said Scrooge.

&ldquo;Without their visits,&rdquo; said the Ghost, &ldquo;you cannot hope to shun the path I tread. Expect the first to-morrow, when the bell tolls One.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Couldn&rsquo;t I take &rsquo;em all at once, and have it over, Jacob?&rdquo; hinted Scrooge.

&ldquo;Expect the second on the next night at the same hour. The third upon the next night when the last stroke of Twelve has ceased to vibrate. Look to see me no more; and look that, for your own sake, you remember what has passed between us!&rdquo;

____________________________________

Spirits of Christmas is a light cooperative strategy game in which players take on the role of the three Spirits of Christmas from the classic novel A Christmas Carol by Charles Dickens. You will be taking the old miser Ebenezer Scrooge on a journey through Christmases of the Past, Present, and Future, showing him the consequences of his actions. Hopefully he will change his ways before he runs out of time!

Players will move Scrooge through scenes from the classic story, taking actions using a simple rondel. Your goal is to present ten pivotal moments in Scrooge's life to the old miser, playing combinations of Spirit cards (Contentment, Compassion, and Charity) to meet the requirements for each Scene. Each action you take will require Scrooge to spend his precious Shillings. You can only convince him to part with 15 Shillings during each journey this night, and if these run out, everyone loses the game.

&mdash;description from the publisher

Sarah Elizabeth Jacobs is known by most as a wife, a member of the local gardening club, an avid patron of the Valley Falls Library, the organist for the First Presbyterian Church of Valley Falls, and a volunteer at the local animal shelter. Because she has so much to live for, it comes as a great shock to everyone who knows her when she is found hanging at the end of a rope in her garage. Even more shocking is the letter pinned to her chest that says simply:
&ldquo;Thou shalt not suffer a witch to live. This one is but the first I have identified as in league with the devil. I will expose the others and any who aid them in the coming days.&rdquo;
The note is signed simply, &ldquo;Witchfinder.&rdquo;
With the promise of more deaths, you must work quickly to identify the Witchfinder and put a stop to this Witch Hunt&hellip;before it&rsquo;s too late. But, move carefully and with great caution as it&rsquo;s now the Season of the Witch!

&mdash;description from the publisher

Forty years ago, John Butterfield designed The Voyage of the BSM Pandora, the first successful solitaire paragraph-driven game. Now this branching narrative game concept goes into a new dimension with Away Team: The Voyages of the Pandora.

Away Team: The Voyages of the Pandora is a game of exploring alien worlds in distant star systems. You command the Pandora, an interstellar survey ship on its voyages of discovery. Each voyage sends Pandora to a different star system where you assemble away teams from the ship&rsquo;s crew and equipment to explore planets, moons and other sites of interest, with the following directives:
- Locate exo-life forms, and document their physiology and behavior;
- Collect exo-DNA, vital to genetic science and human adaptation to life in the stars;
- Identify and survey environments suitable for human settlement and development;
- Search for intelligent life and alien cultures; and if found, establish contact with goodwill;
- Don&rsquo;t get killed.

Away Team has three modes of play.
- The solitaire campaign game, provides an epic inter-connected narrative experience for one player across seven star systems; providing over 80 hours of play time, exploration, and plot-twists.
- The solitaire star system game provides one player with a repeatable play experience commanding one Pandora voyage to a single star system. You set the experience level of your crew and the danger level of each voyage.
- The 2-player game puts players in command of competing away teams from Pandora in a voyage to a single star system, also a repeatable play experience.

-description from publisher

&ldquo;I&rsquo;ve had my fill of smoked fish&rdquo;, the alderman of the little Dutch town grumbles. &ldquo;Bring me some apples to finish the meal!&rdquo;. His servant looks worried. &ldquo;We are out of apples sir. The De Witt family has been cutting peat close to our lands and now the water level in our orchards is too high.&rdquo; The alderman&rsquo;s face turns into a frown: &ldquo;I will go to the count of Holland and file a complaint. The count will surely be on my side.&rdquo; The servant bows and takes his leave. He knows the count has just delegated all water related decisions to a new court close by. The judge presiding is married to De Witt&rsquo;s sister&hellip;

Bailiff of Boscoop is a strategy game set in the late Middle Ages and Early Modern period in Rhineland, part of the county of Holland in what is now The Netherlands. 2-5 players take on the role of local families. Players perform actions in sequence. Family members may claim land. Some may rise to prominence as the founder of a village, as a judge, or as a local duck dealer. The family with the most land at the end of the game wins.

&mdash;description from the publisher

&ldquo;I, Lord Gaston Onomee, invite you to enter the Arena A La Carte. Fire up the ovens. Raid the pantry. Bake delights that would make a connoisseur weep. THEN crush your enemies, see them driven before you. Be the one to taste victory and be the last chef standing in the Baking Battle Royale&rdquo;

Fantasy Food Fight is a &ldquo;take-that&rdquo; style card game where you combine Wet Stuff, Dry Stuff and Tasty Bits to bake dishes. Once a dish is ready, you throw it at another chef, who then draws Splat points. But watch out. Collect 8 Splat points and you&rsquo;re out of the game.  The last chef standing, wins.

Use Cinnamonster cards to defend, steal, glimpse the future, and much more.

The horrible Walking Castles are about to invade the peaceful land of Freigard. Gather the most valiant defenders of this enchanted abode and defeat the relentless mechanical monsters!

Freigard is a deceptively simple game of risk taking and hand management: each turn you have the choice between scoring (if possible) your hand of 3 cards, or draw one extra card (then discard one) in order to improve your hand. If you&rsquo;re too greedy, you risk burning through your deck too fast, but settling down too often might not get you the powerful army you need to defeat the strongest Walking Castles&hellip;

&mdash;description from the publisher

Snowdonia is the scenario-based, worker placement railway-building classic; this special edition boasts gorgeous all-new artwork; faster and easier set-up; and a new scenario - Stockton and Darlington, celebrating the birth of the modern railway 200 years ago.

The special edition differs from the original Snowdonia as follows:
- All new art & Graphic design;
- Upgraded components;
- Has a double-sided board for the two included scenarios (rather than previous card system); and,
- Side A of the board is the Snowdon Mountain Railway; side B is a brand new scenario for the Stockton and Darlington railway.

&ldquo;Ah yes, this is a very interesting piece! Notice the fine craftsmanship, and that you can barely hear the otherworldly wailing emanating from it.&rdquo;

You and up to 3 opponents are rival antiques dealers, each of whom received an invitation to a manor home filled to the brim with very old and valuable collectibles. But when you arrive, you quickly realize that each and every item in the house has one thing in common: they are hopelessly haunted!

Bringing these terrifying treasures back to your warehouse seems like a ghastly idea, but having just a few might raise your profile. Perhaps you can even convince some wealthy collectors to take some of the macabre museum pieces off your hands&hellip;
Your goal is to escape the manor with the least haunted set of loot... that is, if you escape at all!

&mdash;description from the publisher
